      "result": "<task id=\"ses_f0bd32fa4ffe1Sp4hUJ6O6ttna\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have gathered enough evidence. Here is the structured report.\n\n---\n\n# SEARCH FEDERATION SEAM — evidence report (P2.5 / M11a)\n\n## 0. Executive summary\n\nThere are **two distinct server search entry points**, both on `SearchResolver` in `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/`:\n\n1. **`search`** — core full-text search over **object records** (workspace metadata objects), cursor-paginated, returns `SearchRecordDTO` that carries `objectNameSingular` + `recordId`. Implementation: `SearchService` using Postgres `tsvector` + ILIKE fallback over a `searchVector` column.\n2. **`searchAppRecords`** — \"app-provider federation\": runs app-registered `SearchProvider`s and returns `AppSearchRecordDTO` groups. These results carry **only `recordId`, `label`, `description`, `imageUrl`, `path`** — **no `objectNameSingular`**. It groups by installed application.\n\nThe only place they are merged is the **frontend** `SidePanelSearchRecordsPage` (Cmd+K / side-panel search), via `groupSearchResultItems`. There is **no single server-side federated resolver** and **no combined frontend hook**.\n\n**Reuse point for a universal link picker (evidence-based):** the link picker must call the **core `search` path**, i.e. `useObjectRecordSearchRecords` → `SearchDocument`/`search` query (exactly what `SingleRecordPicker`/`useSingleRecordPickerPerformSearch` already does, and what `LinkToRecordPicker` already wires). It cannot use `searchAppRecords` to *create* a link, because `AppSearchRecordDTO` has no `objectNameSingular`/`objectMetadataId` — only an opaque `path`. Details in §5.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Core search implementation\n\n### Resolver / schema\n\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/search.resolver.ts`\n- `@CoreResolver()`, guarded by `WorkspaceAuthGuard` + `CustomPermissionGuard`, filtered by `SearchApiExceptionFilter` (lines 24-32).\n- `search(...)` at **line 39-93**: `@Query(() => SearchResultConnectionDTO)`. Args: `searchInput`, `limit`, `filter`, `includedObjectNameSingulars`, `excludedObjectNameSingulars`, `after` (line 42-50).\n- Flow: loads `flatObjectMetadataMaps`/`flatFieldMetadataMaps` (line 53-59) → `searchService.filterObjectMetadataItems` (line 65-70) → `getAllRecordsWithObjectMetadataItems` (line 72-82) → `computeSearchObjectResults` (line 84-92).\n\n### Input type — `SearchArgs`\n\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/dtos/search-args.ts:7-35`\n```\n@ArgsType() SearchArgs {\n  searchInput: string;                         // required\n  limit: number;                               // Int, Max(100)\n  after?: string;                              // cursor\n  includedObjectNameSingulars?: string[];\n  filter?: ObjectRecordFilterInput;\n  excludedObjectNameSingulars?: string[];\n}\n```\n\nFrontend counterpart `SEARCH_QUERY` in `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu/graphql/queries/search.ts:3-37`; generated as `SearchDocument` / `SearchQuery` in `packages/twenty-front/src/generated/graphql.ts:903-913,1099`.\n\n### Output types\n\n- `SearchResultConnectionDTO { edges: SearchResultEdgeDTO[]; pageInfo }` — `dtos/search-result-connection.dto.ts:6-13`\n- `SearchResultEdgeDTO { node: SearchRecordDTO; cursor: string }` — `dtos/search-result-edge.dto.ts:5-12`\n- `SearchRecordDTO` — `dtos/search-record.dto.ts:7-38`: `recordId`, **`objectNameSingular`**, `objectLabelSingular`, `label`, `imageUrl`, `tsRankCD`, `tsRank`.\n\n### How it federates across object metadata\n\n`SearchService` (`services/search.service.ts`):\n- `getAllRecordsWithObjectMetadataItems` (line 81-151) iterates **every filtered `flatObjectMetadata`**, in chunks of 5 (`OBJECT_METADATA_ITEMS_CHUNK_SIZE`, line 68), and runs the search query per object under the caller's role config (`resolveRolePermissionConfig`, line 114-119) with `workspaceOrmManager.getRepository(objectNameSingular, rolePermissionConfig)` (line 121-125).\n- `filterObjectMetadataItems` (line 153-196):\n  - Always drops `!isActive` (line 166-168).\n  - **Explicit inclusion branch** (line 170-183): if `includedObjectNameSingulars.length > 0`, returns objects in the included list minus excluded, **skipping the `isSearchable` check** (but dropping `OBJECTS_WITH_CHANNEL_VISIBILITY_CONSTRAINTS`).\n  - **Default branch** (line 185-193): requires `isSearchable` and not excluded.\n- The actual lookups (`buildSearchQueryAndGetRecords`, line 260-374) use:\n  - `ts_rank_cd(\"searchVector\", to_tsquery('simple', unaccent(...)))` (line 313-315), `WHERE \"searchVector\" @@ to_tsquery(...)` (line 342-353), GIN-backed.\n  - ILIKE fallback only when tsvector yields zero on the first page (`buildSearchQueryAndGetRecordsWithFallback`, line 203-258; `buildIlikeFallbackQuery`, line 376-500) — and this fallback also matches against `\"searchVector\"::text` (line 467).\n- Merge/rank: `computeSearchObjectResults` (line 778-870) flattens all objects, resolves label/image, sorts by `tsRankCD` then `tsRank` then `STANDARD_OBJECTS_BY_PRIORITY_RANK` (`constants/standard-objects-by-priority-rank.ts:2-8`: person 5, company 4, opportunity 3, note 2, task 1).\n\n### Does it support all objects or only some?\n\nEffectively **only objects that are `isSearchable` and have a populated `searchVector`**:\n- `searchVector` (TS_VECTOR system field) + GIN index is auto-provisioned for **every** custom/app object on create (`metadata-side-effect/.../object-search-vector-on-create-side-effect-handler.service.ts:36-61`).\n- But the `searchFieldMetadata` row that *populates* `searchVector` is created **only when `flatObjectMetadata.isSearchable === true`** and the label identifier is a searchable field type (same handler, line 95-97, 126-131). A non-searchable object has a `NULL` `searchVector`, so both the tsvector query and the ILIKE fallback match nothing.\n- `includedObjectNameSingulars` bypasses the `isSearchable` filter (line 170-183) but cannot resurrect a NULL index.\n- Every object must have a label identifier or `getLabelIdentifierColumns` throws `LABEL_IDENTIFIER_FIELD_NOT_FOUND` (line 550-559).\n\nApp-owned objects **are** included by default: the app-manifest converter defaults `isSearchable` to true (`application/application-manifest/converters/from-object-manifest-to-universal-flat-object-metadata.util.ts:40` — `objectManifest.isSearchable ?? true`). `defineObject` exposes `isSearchable?: boolean` (`packages/twenty-shared/src/application/objectManifestType.ts:16`). The A2E projects/documents objects don't set it, so they are searchable.\n\n---\n\n## 2. `searchAppRecords` specifically\n\n**Defined in the server only** (not twenty-sdk, not apps):\n- Resolver: `search.resolver.ts:95-117`\n  ```\n  @Query(() => [AppSearchResultGroupDTO])\n  async searchAppRecords(@Args('searchInput', { type: () => String }) searchInput: string)\n  ```\n  It loads `flatApplicationMaps` and passes `Object.keys(flatApplicationMaps.idByUniversalIdentifier)` to the service as installed apps (line 110-116).\n- Service: `services/app-search.service.ts`:\n  - `MAX_RECORDS_PER_APP = 5` (line 10).\n  - `searchInstalledAppRecords` (line 22-78): keeps only providers whose `appUniversalIdentifier` is in the installed set (line 31-37), runs each `provider.search({searchInput, limit, workspaceId})` (line 46-50), maps to `AppSearchRecordDTO`, drops empty groups, and try/catches each provider so one failure can't break the payload (line 65-72).\n\n**Input/output types:**\n- Input: a bare `String!` `searchInput`. The front document is hand-written (no generated document): `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/pages/search/graphql/queries/searchAppRecords.ts:6-18` — `query SearchAppRecords($searchInput: String!)`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/dtos/app-search-result-group.dto.ts:6-14` — `AppSearchResultGroupDTO { appUniversalIdentifier: string; records: AppSearchRecordDTO[] }`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/dtos/app-search-record.dto.ts:8-27` — `AppSearchRecordDTO { recordId: UUID; label: string; description?: string; imageUrl?: string; path: string }`. **No `objectNameSingular`, no object metadata id.**\n- Provider contract: `types/search-provider.type.ts:1-23` — `SearchProviderParams { searchInput; limit; workspaceId }`, `SearchProviderResultItem { recordId; label; description?; imageUrl?; path }`.\n\n**Registration / federation mechanism:**\n- `@RegisteredSearchProvider({ appUniversalIdentifier })` decorator (`decorators/registered-search-provider.decorator.ts:15-20`) applies `@Injectable()` and `Reflect.defineMetadata`.\n- `SearchProviderRegistryService` (`services/search-provider-registry.service.ts`) scans Nest providers in `onModuleInit` via `DiscoveryService` (line 27-63) and stores them per app id (line 20-23).\n- Providers are registered as ordinary Nest providers in **`search.module.ts:21-28`** — currently exactly two: `DocumentSearchProviderService` and `A2eProjectsSearchProviderService`.\n- The two live providers:\n  - `services/document-search-provider.service.ts:20-21,39-41` — app id `19126a9c-…`; ILIKE over `document.title` where `archivedAt: null`; `path: /object/documents/<id>` (line 108).\n  - `services/a2e-projects-search-provider.service.ts:20-21,62-64` — app id `4f759655-…`; ILIKE over standard `task.title` + app `project.name` (archived excluded); `path: /object/<singular>/<id>` (line 145, 154).\n\n**What it searches:** only whatever the registered provider's own hard-coded query selects; it is not object-metadata-driven. Apps cannot self-register a Nest provider (documented in `.ralph-tui/iterations/d04cf6b4_2026-09-18_22-29-31_P5.2-chat-live.log:331`: \"apps can't add Nest providers to the core server\"), so app-provider federation is **server-hardcoded today**.\n\nPrior known bug fixed (US-008): providers passed a plain `{ ilike }` object instead of a TypeORM `ILike` `FindOperator`, so the workspace ORM compiled equality and returned `[]` silently (`docs/plan/phases/phase-04-report.md:725`; providers now use `ILike`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Command-menu / global search frontend that lists records across objects\n\nThe Cmd+K surface is the **side-panel `SearchRecords` page**, not a `modules/command-menu` search page.\n\n- Hotkey → open search page: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu/hooks/useCommandMenuHotKeys.ts:14,35` calls `openRecordsSearchPage`; opener `modules/side-panel/hooks/useOpenRecordsSearchPageInSidePanel.ts:13-21` navigates to `SidePanelPages.SearchRecords`.\n- Page registered at `modules/side-panel/constants/SidePanelPagesConfig.tsx:31,60`.\n- **`SidePanelSearchRecordsPage`** (`modules/side-panel/pages/search/components/SidePanelSearchRecordsPage.tsx:45`): the actual cross-object aggregator. It composes:\n  - `useSidePanelSearchRecords()` — core object records (line 46-47)\n  - `useAppSearchResultItems()` — app-provider groups (line 48-51)\n  - `useChatSearchResultItems()` (line 52-55), `useDriveSearchResultItems()` (line 56-59), `useHelpSearchResultItems()` (line 60-62)\n  - merges via `groupSearchResultItems` at line 86-95.\n- **Core fetch hook: `useObjectRecordSearchRecords`** (`modules/object-record/hooks/useObjectRecordSearchRecords.ts:27-67`) — runs `SearchDocument` with `variables: { searchInput, limit (default 30 from MAX_SEARCH_RESULTS), filter, includedObjectNameSingulars: objectNameSingulars }` (line 40-51) on `apolloCoreClient`; exposes `searchRecords` (line 57-60). Its return node type is `SearchRecordDTO`, which includes `objectNameSingular`.\n- **Searchable object list:** `useSidePanelSearchRecords` (line 23-72) uses `useSearchableObjectNameSingulars` (`modules/side-panel/hooks/useSearchableObjectNameSingulars.ts:12-32`) → all readable objects filtered by `isSearchable` (or hidden-objects toggle).\n- **App fetch hook: `useAppSearchResultItems`** (`modules/side-panel/pages/search/hooks/useAppSearchResultItems.ts:29-85`) — `useQuery(SEARCH_APP_RECORDS_QUERY)` with `fetchPolicy: 'no-cache'`, flattens groups into `GroupableSearchResultItem` and sets **`objectNameSingular: ''`** (line 67) and `groupKey: 'app:<appUniversalIdentifier>'` (line 74).\n- **Grouping/ranking util:** `modules/side-panel/pages/search/utils/groupSearchResultItems.ts` — `GroupableSearchResultItem` (line 11-17; `path?` present on app results), sort by frecency then fold into per-group buckets (line 21-59).\n- **Click handling** (`SidePanelSearchRecordsPage.tsx:148-180`): if `item.path` is defined → `openRoutedPageInSidePanel` (fallback `navigate(path)`); else if task/note → `openRecordInSidePanel`; else `navigate(getAppPath(AppPath.RecordShowPage, { objectNameSingular, objectRecordId }))`.\n\nNote on naming: the symbols you asked about are `SidePanelSearchRecordsPage` (not `SearchRecordsPage`) and `useObjectRecordSearchRecords`/`useSearchableObjectNameSingulars` (there is no `useSearchRecords`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. How a \"Link…\" fallback / record picker picks a target record today\n\n- **`LinkToRecordPicker`** (`modules/blocknote-editor/components/LinkToRecordPicker.tsx`):\n  - Builds the target list from `useFilteredObjectMetadataItems()` + `useObjectPermissions()` (line 35-36), then `filterReadableActiveObjectMetadataItems(...).filter((item) => !item.isSystem && item.isSearchable)` (line 38-45); `filterReadableActiveObjectMetadataItems` (`modules/object-metadata/utils/filterReadableActiveObjectMetadataItems.ts:5-25`) keeps `isActive` and `canReadObjectRecords`.\n  - Passes the resulting `objectNameSingulars` into **`SingleRecordPicker`** (line 96-102).\n  - On selection, inserts a blocknote `mention` with `recordId` + `objectMetadataId` + `objectNameSingular` + fallback `label` (line 51-85) — note it uses `objectMetadataItem.labelSingular` as the label, **not the search result's `label`**.\n  - Opened by the slash-menu item `LinkToRecordSlashMenuItem.tsx:27-57` (\"Link to record\", group `links`).\n- **`SingleRecordPicker`** (`modules/object-record/record-picker/single-record-picker/components/SingleRecordPicker.tsx:21-94`) renders `SingleRecordPickerMenuItemsWithSearch`, which calls `useSingleRecordPickerRecords` (`.../hooks/useSingleRecordPickerRecords.ts:20-27`) → **`useSingleRecordPickerPerformSearch`** (`.../hooks/useSingleRecordPickerPerformSearch.ts:16-169`).\n  - `useSingleRecordPickerPerformSearch` runs **three** `useObjectRecordSearchRecords` calls: selected records (line 64-70), filtered-selected (line 72-80), and the actual search with `objectNameSingulars: readableObjectNameSingulars`, `searchInput: searchFilter`, `limit` (line 86-93); produces `RecordPickerPickableMorphItem { recordId, objectMetadataId, … }` (line 128-160).\n- **Relation picker** (single relation field): `RelationManyToOneFieldInput.tsx:107-126` passes `objectNameSingulars={[fieldDefinition.metadata.relationObjectMetadataNameSingular]}` (a **single** target object) plus `onCreate`/`onMorphItemSelected` into the same `SingleRecordPicker`. So today, relation and link pickers are the same component parameterized by `objectNameSingulars[]`; only `objectNameSingulars` differs (one target vs. all searchable objects).\n- Multi-relation uses the parallel `MultipleRecordPicker` (`modules/object-record/record-picker/multiple-record-picker/`), also driven by `useObjectRecordSearchRecords`.\n\n**Key observation:** `SingleRecordPicker` is already \"universal\" over objects; the missing piece for a universal link picker is not the picker but (a) persisting a link (junction) and (b) optionally surfacing app-provider results. `RecordPickerPickableMorphItem` requires `objectMetadataId`, which app-provider results cannot supply.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Is there a single federated entry point? Documented gaps? Reuse point\n\n### Is there one?\n\n- **Server:** No. `search` and `searchAppRecords` are two separate `@Query`s (`search.resolver.ts:39` and `:97`). `search` is metadata-driven; `searchAppRecords` is provider-driven and install-gated.\n- **Frontend:** No single hook. The only merge is inline in `SidePanelSearchRecordsPage.tsx:86-95` (`groupSearchResultItems` over core + app + chat + drive + help). There is no `useFederatedSearch`.\n- **Blueprint intent:** `docs/plan/03-integration-blueprint.md:175-183` — \"Existing search provider interface/decorator registry discovers Nest providers; `AppSearchService` gates by installed app IDs… Cmd+K results grouped by app… Deep links: every result opens … using stable URLs (`/object/<name>/<id>`, app routes).\"\n- **Roadmap intent:** `PLAN.md:404-409` (M11a, unchecked) \"Universal link picker & 'Related' panel. From any record or page: 'Link…' searches all objects (reuse search federation, P2.5) and creates a link via a generic junction…\". `PLAN.md:1201-1217` is P2.5 Global search v1 (only the perf budget line remains unchecked).\n\n### Gaps a link picker must account for\n\n1. **`searchAppRecords` results cannot create links.** `AppSearchRecordDTO` exposes only `path` (no `objectNameSingular`/`objectMetadataId`); `useAppSearchResultItems.ts:67` even sets `objectNameSingular: ''`. `RecordPickerPickableMorphItem` (used by both pickers) requires `objectMetadataId`. So app-provider hits are navigable but not link-addressable.\n2. **Core `search` only returns records for objects with a populated `searchVector`,** i.e. `isSearchable` objects with a searchable label identifier — a non-searchable object yields nothing even if explicitly included (§1).\n3. **App search providers are server-hardcoded** in `search.module.ts:21-28`; the SDK/apps cannot register one (`.ralph-tui/.../P5.2-chat-live.log:331`). The `searchAppRecords` live path has a standing Tier-2 re-proof gap (`PLAN.md:1212`, `PLAN.md:1215-1217`; `docs/plan/phases/phase-04-report.md:566,730`).\n4. **Preview gap:** the app-provider results are excluded from the Cmd+K record preview because they have `path`, not object metadata — `isSearchResultItemPreviewable.ts:9-13` plus the gate at `SidePanelSearchRecordsPage.tsx:126-131`. Phase-01 report notes this explicitly (`docs/plan/phases/phase-01-report.md:310` gotcha 4).\n5. **`LinkToRecordPicker` uses `labelSingular` as the mention label** (line 79), not the matched record `label`; a universal picker should preserve the record label.\n6. Core search is a **`@CoreResolver`** requiring a workspace auth context and caller-scoped role permissions; it is not a public/unauthenticated index.\n\n### Clear statement — the reuse point a universal link picker should call\n\nFor selecting a record to link, the reusable entry point is the **core `search` query**, not `searchAppRecords`:\n\n- Frontend call: **`useObjectRecordSearchRecords({ objectNameSingulars, searchInput, filter, limit })`** (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useObjectRecordSearchRecords.ts:27`), which issues **`SearchDocument`** (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu/graphql/queries/search.ts:3`; generated `SearchDocument` at `packages/twenty-front/src/generated/graphql.ts:1099`).\n- Server query: **`search`** on `SearchResolver` (`search.resolver.ts:39`), backed by `SearchService` (`services/search.service.ts`).\n- The picker UI to reuse is **`SingleRecordPicker`** with `objectNameSingulars` = all readable, active, `isSearchable`, non-system objects (today computed in `LinkToRecordPicker.tsx:38-45` via `useSearchableObjectNameSingulars`/`filterReadableActiveObjectMetadataItems`), selected through `useSingleRecordPickerPerformSearch` (`.../useSingleRecordPickerPerformSearch.ts:16`).\n- If app-provider groups must also appear in the same list, they can be merged for *display* via `useAppSearchResultItems` + `groupSearchResultItems` (as `SidePanelSearchRecordsPage.tsx` does), but **link creation must key off the core `SearchRecordDTO.objectNameSingular` + `recordId`** (resolving `objectMetadataId` from object metadata), because `AppSearchRecordDTO` carries only `path`.\n\n**Net:** the single federated *display* entry point today is the frontend aggregation in `SidePanelSearchRecordsPage`; the single federated *link-addressable* entry point is the core `search` query (`useObjectRecordSearchRecords`/`SearchDocument`). A universal link picker should reuse the latter for target selection and may layer the former for app-provider suggestions.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
