        "spawnedAt": "2026-09-30T21:19:30.115Z",
        "prompt": "You are researching the Twenty/A2E codebase at /Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite. Read-only research task — do not modify anything. I need an evidence-based report on the \"Related\" widget surface options and the M8d backlink precedent.\n\nFind and report:\n1. Page-layout widget system: the widget types available (packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/... — enums like `WidgetType`, `WidgetConfigurationType`, record-table/widget renderers). What widget types exist (TABLE/KANBAN/LIST/CALENDAR/FILES/NOTES/RELATION/etc.)? Can an app-owned/custom widget be added, or must one of the built-in widget types be used? Cite the `RecordTableWidgetRendererContent` dispatch and the widget type enums.\n2. The native relation/related-list widget: how does a record page show related records from a relation field today? Find the `FIELD`/`RELATION` widget or `FieldWidget` that renders a one-to-many relation as a table. Cite it.\n3. M8d \"backlinks\" — grep for `backlink`, `Backlink`, `back-link`, and any document backlink feature (likely in packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor or a2e-documents app). What is M8d exactly per PLAN.md? Search PLAN.md for M8d. What UI/component currently renders backlinks, if any?\n4. App front components: can an internal app register a page-layout widget, or only front components/tabs? Look at packages/twenty-apps/internal/* for `front-components` and any page-layout/widget registration in application configs. Report what surfaces an app can own (page layout tab, widget, front component).\n5. The `PageLayoutWidget` entity/object: is `widget` a standard object that apps can create records for, or is it host-only? Cite the object definition.\n\nReturn a structured report: the available widget surfaces, whether the \"Related\" panel should be a page-layout widget vs an app front component, with file:line citations and constraints. Be specific and quote real symbols. Do NOT write code.",
