        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f0bd32f72ffeo433MaGC9oz5Pj\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have gathered comprehensive evidence. Here is the structured report.\n\n---\n\n# Evidence-Based Report: \"Related\" Widget Surface Options & M8d Backlink Precedent\n\nRoot: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite`. All citations are `file:line`. Research is read-only; nothing was modified.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Page-layout widget system\n\n### 1a. The widget type enum is a closed, server-owned union — no RELATION/KANBAN/LIST types\n\n`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/page-layout/WidgetType.ts:1-27` defines the canonical enum:\n\n```\nVIEW, IFRAME, FIELD, FIELDS, GRAPH, STANDALONE_RICH_TEXT, TIMELINE, TASKS, NOTES,\nFILES, EMAILS, CALENDAR, FIELD_RICH_TEXT, WORKFLOW, WORKFLOW_VERSION, WORKFLOW_RUN,\nFRONT_COMPONENT, RECORD_TABLE, EMAIL_THREAD, CALL_RECORDING_SUMMARY,\nCALL_RECORDING_TRANSCRIPT, MESSAGE_CAMPAIGN_BODY, MESSAGE_CAMPAIGN_DETAILS,\nFORM_FIELD, DISCUSSIONS\n```\n\nImportant: there is **no `RELATION`, `KANBAN`, `LIST`, `GALLERY`, or custom widget type**. `KANBAN/LIST/CALENDAR/TABLE` are *view layouts* rendered inside a `RECORD_TABLE` (or `VIEW`) widget, not widget types. There is no `FORM_FIELD`-vs-`RELATION` relation widget; relation display is a *display mode* of `FIELD` (see §2).\n\nThe server mirrors it exactly in `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/page-layout-widget/enums/widget-configuration-type.type.ts:7-36` (`WidgetConfigurationType`). The generated GraphQL `WidgetConfigurationType` union is frozen at `packages/twenty-client-sdk/src/metadata/generated/schema.ts:768`.\n\nThe configuration payload union is `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/page-layout/page-layout-widget-configuration.type.ts:206-234` (`PageLayoutWidgetConfiguration`), with `FieldConfiguration` at `:100-109` and `FrontComponentConfiguration` at `:140-144`.\n\n### 1b. The renderer dispatch\n\nTwo dispatch layers:\n\n**Top-level widget dispatch** — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/components/WidgetContentRenderer.tsx:29-102`. A `switch (widget.type)` maps every `WidgetType` to a renderer, including:\n- `case WidgetType.FIELD: return <FieldWidget .../>` (`:39-40`)\n- `case WidgetType.RECORD_TABLE: return <RecordTableWidgetRenderer .../>` (`:81-82`)\n- `case WidgetType.FRONT_COMPONENT: return <FrontComponentWidgetRenderer .../>` (`:78-79`)\n- `default: return null` (`:99-100`)\n\n**View-layout dispatch inside RECORD_TABLE/FIELD-table** — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/record-table/components/RecordTableWidgetRendererContent.tsx:84-96`:\n\n```ts\nconst renderWidgetForLayout = {\n  [ViewType.TABLE]:   () => <RecordTableWidget .../>,\n  [ViewType.KANBAN]:  () => <RecordBoardWidget .../>,\n  [ViewType.LIST]:    () => <RecordListWidget />,\n  [ViewType.CALENDAR]:() => <RecordCalendarWidget .../>,\n} satisfies Record<RecordTableWidgetLayout, () => ReactNode>;\n```\n\nThe keyed object (rather than a chain) is a deliberate compile-time exhaustiveness guard (`:82-83`).\n\n### 1c. Can an app-owned/custom widget be added?\n\n**No new widget type.** The server enum is authority: the entity column types on `WidgetType` (`page-layout-widget.entity.ts:72-78`), the field-type validator whitelist (`flat-page-layout-widget-type-validator.service.ts:55-186`), and the app manifest converter cast `type: pageLayoutWidgetManifest.type as WidgetType` (`from-page-layout-widget-manifest-to-universal-flat-page-layout-widget.util.ts:84`). An app manifest that names an unknown type is cast, not validated to a new behavior; nothing in the front dispatcher would render it.\n\n**The one app-authored widget surface is `FRONT_COMPONENT`.** It is a built-in `WidgetType` whose configuration points at an app-owned front component (`FrontComponentConfiguration`, `page-layout-widget-configuration.type.ts:140-144`) and is rendered by `FrontComponentWidgetRenderer` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/front-component/components/FrontComponentWidgetRenderer.tsx:37-71`), which lazily loads `@/front-components/components/FrontComponentRenderer` and passes `selectedRecordIds` from `targetRecordIdentifier` (`:54-56, :64-68`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. The native relation / related-list widget\n\nThere is **no `RELATION` widget**; a one-to-many relation is rendered by the **`FIELD` widget** (`type: 'FIELD'`) using its `fieldDisplayMode`. `FieldConfiguration` is at `page-layout-widget-configuration.type.ts:100-109`:\n\n```ts\nexport type FieldConfiguration = {\n  configurationType: 'FIELD';\n  fieldMetadataId: string;\n  fieldDisplayMode: 'CARD' | 'EDITOR' | 'FIELD' | 'VIEW' | 'TABLE';\n  viewId?: string;\n  nestedRelationFieldMetadataId?: string | null;\n  isUIEditable?: boolean;\n};\n```\n\n`FieldDisplayMode` values are confirmed at `packages/twenty-front/src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts:2020-2026`.\n\n`FieldWidget` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/field/components/FieldWidget.tsx`) is the dispatcher:\n- Relation branch: `if (isFieldRelation(fieldDefinition)) { ... }` (`:128`)\n- **`FieldDisplayMode.TABLE` → `FieldWidgetRelationTable`** (`:184-190` for plain relations; `:155-163` for junction relations)\n- `CARD` → `FieldWidgetRelationCard` / `FieldWidgetJunctionRelationCard` (`:144-152, :174-182`)\n- default → `FieldWidgetRelationField` (record chips) (`:193-199`)\n\n`FieldWidgetRelationTable` is the \"related records as a table\" renderer: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/field/components/FieldWidgetRelationTable.tsx:44-261`. It computes the relation target object (`:68-136`), builds a `filterCurrentRecord` from the page record (`:208-230`), and delegates to the shared table:\n\n```tsx\n<RecordTableWidgetRendererContent\n  objectMetadataId={tableObjectMetadataId}\n  viewId={viewId}\n  widgetId={widget.id}\n  ...\n/>\n```\n(`:248-257`). Default is editable on record pages (`:60-63`).\n\nSo today a record page lists related records from **a declared relation field** via `FIELD` + `TABLE`; `FieldWidgetRelationField` renders the compact chip list for `FIELD`/default modes (`FieldWidgetRelationField.tsx:13-43`). Other relation-shaped built-ins read a fixed native relation by widget type via `WidgetTypeToRelationFieldName` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/constants/WidgetTypeToRelationFieldName.ts:3-15`: `TASKS→taskTargets`, `NOTES→noteTargets`, `FILES→attachments`, `TIMELINE→timelineActivities`, `DISCUSSIONS→discussions`, …) and `WidgetTypesRequiringRelationField` (`WidgetTypesRequiringRelationField.ts:7-13`).\n\nThere is no generic \"list everything that references me\" widget — that is what M8d/M11a must build.\n\n---\n\n## 3. M8d \"backlinks\" — what it is and what exists today\n\n### 3a. M8d is *planned only*; nothing is implemented\n\n`PLAN.md:316-318`:\n\n> **M8d — Backlinks & mentions panel.** \"Mentioned in\" section on document and on every record page (page-layout tab/widget) computed from mention nodes stored at save; no full-text scan at read.\n\nRelated: `PLAN.md:185` (G9 — editor has \"no page icon/cover/backlinks\"), `PLAN.md:189` (G13 — \"no generic 'link any record' / backlink panel\", fixed by M11a), `PLAN.md:404-409` (M11a — \"Record pages show a 'Related' widget listing links + backlinks (M8d)\"), `PLAN.md:428` (E14 acceptance: \"backlink visible on task\"), `PLAN.md:431` (E17).\n\n### 3b. No backlink UI/component currently exists\n\nRepo-wide searches for `backlink|Backlink|back-link|mentionedIn|Mentioned in|backLinks` return **only docs/plan prose** — no implementation:\n- No matches in `packages/twenty-apps/**` (search of the app tree).\n- No matches in `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor`.\n- The only source-adjacent hit is an unrelated migration comment (`optimistically-apply-create-action...util.ts:56`).\n- User docs explicitly mark it unshipped: `packages/twenty-docs/user-guide/a2e-suite/working-across-apps.mdx:8-10,24-27` (\"The universal link picker and Related panel (M11a) are **not shipped yet**; linking today is per-pair\") and `:33` (\"Read the Related panel\" is listed under *Planned sections*).\n\nThe M11a spike deliverable is only *claimed*: `docs/plan/phases/phase-15-report.md:1-3` contains a single CLAIMED line, and `tasks/prd.json:503-518` (US-125) has `\"passes\": false`. US-125 scope explicitly defers the decision: `tasks/prd.json:510` — \"Decide the search-federation reuse point … and the **'Related' widget surface (page-layout widget vs front component)**\".\n\n### 3c. The data foundation that *does* exist: mention nodes are stored at save\n\n`MentionInlineContent` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/blocks/MentionInlineContent.tsx:84-104`) is a BlockNote inline content spec whose `propSchema` stores, per mention: `recordId`, `objectMetadataId`, `objectNameSingular`, `label`, `imageUrl` (`:87-103`). New notes store `objectNameSingular + label + imageUrl` directly (`:116-128`); legacy notes only `objectMetadataId + recordId` and resolve lazily (`:28-82, :130-136`). It is registered in the editor schema at `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/blocks/Schema.ts:33` (`mention: MentionInlineContent`).\n\nMentions are inserted by `LinkToRecordPicker` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/components/LinkToRecordPicker.tsx:72-84`), which writes a `mention` node with `recordId/objectMetadataId/objectNameSingular/label`. This is precisely the \"mention nodes stored at save\" that M8d says to compute backlinks from — but **nothing yet indexes or queries them for backlinks** (no denormalized junction/table, no \"Mentioned in\" query).\n\n---\n\n## 4. What surfaces can an internal app own?\n\n### 4a. Apps declare `pageLayouts` and `pageLayoutTabs`; widgets are **nested**, not independently syncable\n\nThe manifest types are `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/pageLayoutManifestType.ts:11-35`:\n- `PageLayoutWidgetManifest` (`:11-18`) — `type: \\`${WidgetType}\\`` + `configuration: PageLayoutWidgetUniversalConfiguration`\n- `PageLayoutTabManifest` (`:20-27`) — `widgets?: PageLayoutWidgetManifest[]`\n- `PageLayoutManifest` (`:29-35`) — `tabs?: PageLayoutTabManifest[]`\n\nThe server confirms widgets exist **only as children** of a tab: the widget descriptor's `getCandidates` walks `pageLayoutTabs[].widgets` and `pageLayouts[].tabs[].widgets` (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-manifest/utils/find-manifest-entity-descriptor-by-universal-identifier.util.ts:117-129`), and the converter requires a `pageLayoutTabUniversalIdentifier` plus `applicationUniversalIdentifier` (`from-page-layout-widget-manifest-to-universal-flat-page-layout-widget.util.ts:62-100`).\n\nCrucially, the **syncable entity enum has `PageLayout` and `PageLayoutTab` but no `PageLayoutWidget`** (`packages/twenty-shared/src/application/enums/syncable-entities.enum.ts:13-14`). So there is no top-level \"widget\" entity an app registers; it ships widgets as part of a layout/tab it declares.\n\n### 4b. The only app-code-backed widget type is `FRONT_COMPONENT`\n\nReal precedents in `packages/twenty-apps/internal/`:\n\n- **`a2e-documents`** declares its document record page with a `FRONT_COMPONENT` widget bound to the app's own `document-page` front component:\n  `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/page-layouts/document.page-layout.ts:37-45`:\n  ```ts\n  { title: 'Page', type: 'FRONT_COMPONENT',\n    configuration: { configurationType: 'FRONT_COMPONENT',\n                     frontComponentUniversalIdentifier: FRONT_COMPONENT_IDS.documentPage } }\n  ```\n  The component (`.../front-components/document-page.front-component.tsx:825-831`) already renders app-owned page chrome (breadcrumbs, icon/cover, outline, child pages) and reads the host-supplied record via `useSelectedRecordIds()` (`:275-279`). It uses `defineFrontComponent` and the `twenty-sdk/front-component` runtime.\n\n- **`a2e-chat`** takes the *additive* route: instead of overriding a whole record page, it declares a standalone tab on an existing standard page layout:\n  `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-chat/src/page-layout-tabs/company-discussions.page-layout-tab.ts:15-35` — `pageLayoutUniversalIdentifier: STANDARD_PAGE_LAYOUT.companyRecordPage.universalIdentifier`, with a `DISCUSSIONS` widget. Its comment (`:10-14`) notes a standalone tab is \"additive) rather than shipping an app page layout, which would override every default company tab.\"\n\n- **`rich-app` fixture** shows the same nested pattern with a `FRONT_COMPONENT` and a `GRAPH` widget in a standalone tab (`packages/twenty-apps/fixtures/rich-app/src/page-layout-tabs/extra-tab.page-layout-tab.ts:16-39`).\n\n### 4c. Host UI for adding widgets (what a user/editor can insert)\n\n`SidePanelPageLayoutRecordPageWidgetTypeSelect.tsx:353-405` offers only: **Fields group** (`FIELDS`), **Field** (`FIELD`), **Note**, and a **Front Components** section populated from installed non-headless front components (`:142-155, :383-404`). A `FRONT_COMPONENT` widget is created with `type: WidgetType.FRONT_COMPONENT` and `configuration.frontComponentId` (`:298-312`). `RecordPageAddWidgetSection.tsx:77-108` mirrors `Fields group` / `Field` / `Note` / \"More widgets\". So the host itself treats an app front component as a first-class insertable widget.\n\n### 4d. Surfaces an app can own — summary\n\n| Surface | Ownable by app? | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Navigation item / command menu | Yes | `a2e-documents/src/navigation-menu-items/*`, `command-menu-items/*` |\n| Front component (headless or UI) | Yes | `defineFrontComponent` (`document-page...tsx:825`) |\n| Page layout (record page; **replaces** default) | Yes | `document.page-layout.ts:11-64`; warning in `document-generator/.../document-record.page-layout.ts:13-16` |\n| Page layout **tab** (additive on standard layout) | Yes | `company-discussions.page-layout-tab.ts:10-35` |\n| Widget **nested in** own tab/layout, type must be built-in | Yes | `pageLayoutManifestType.ts:20-25`; `syncable-entities.enum.ts:13-14` |\n| New/arbitrary widget **type** | No | `WidgetType.ts` closed enum; `page-layout-widget.entity.ts:72-78` |\n| App-code-backed widget payload | Yes, only via `FRONT_COMPONENT` | `FrontComponentWidgetRenderer.tsx:37-71` |\n\n---\n\n## 5. The `PageLayoutWidget` entity/object — host-owned metadata, not an app workspace object\n\nEntity: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/page-layout-widget/entities/page-layout-widget.entity.ts`\n- `@Entity({ name: 'pageLayoutWidget', schema: 'core' })` (`:41`) — it is a **core metadata entity**, not a workspace object.\n- `type: WidgetType` enum column (`:72-78`); `configuration: jsonb` (`:102-105`).\n- It extends `OverridableEntity` (`:54`) → `SyncableEntity` (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/types/overridable-entity.ts:6-14`), which carries `universalIdentifier` and `applicationId` (`syncable-entity.interface.ts:9-21`). So widgets are application-scoped and can be app-overridable (`overrides` column), but the object itself is host-defined.\n\nIt is managed through the **metadata GraphQL API**, not the workspace data API:\n`packages/twenty-client-sdk/src/metadata/generated/schema.graphql:3546-3547` (`getPageLayoutWidgets`, `getPageLayoutWidget`), `:3839-3841` (`createPageLayoutWidget`, `updatePageLayoutWidget`, `destroyPageLayoutWidget`); input shapes at `:4475-4484` (`CreatePageLayoutWidgetInput` requires `type: WidgetType`, `configuration: JSON`). There is no workspace-GraphQL query for `pageLayoutWidget` records — apps use `CoreApiClient` for workspace objects, and `definePageLayout`/`definePageLayoutTab` for metadata. An app therefore does **not** create arbitrary widget records; it declares them in its manifest (nested, built-in type only).\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion: page-layout widget vs. app front component for \"Related\"\n\n### The available surfaces for a \"Related\" panel\n\n1. **A native page-layout widget** is impossible as a *new* type (closed `WidgetType`). It can only be one of the built-ins:\n   - `FIELD` + `fieldDisplayMode: TABLE` renders **one declared relation** as a table (`FieldWidget.tsx:184-190` → `FieldWidgetRelationTable.tsx:248`). It cannot express \"all links + backlinks\" because that set is not a single declared relation and has no `fieldMetadataId`.\n   - `RECORD_TABLE` renders one object's view (`RecordTableWidgetRendererContent.tsx:84-96`), filtered by the current record; it also cannot aggregate heterogeneous backlinks.\n2. **A `FRONT_COMPONENT` widget** — an app ships a front component and declares it nested in a page-layout/tab (`FrontComponentConfiguration`, `page-layout-widget-configuration.type.ts:140-144`; rendered by `FrontComponentWidgetRenderer.tsx:37-71`). It receives the current record id (`:54-56`) and can query arbitrary objects via `CoreApiClient`. This is the only surface that can *host app logic* inside a widget.\n3. **An app-owned page-layout tab** on a standard record page (additive), as `a2e-chat` does (`company-discussions.page-layout-tab.ts:10-35`; standard ids exported via `standard-page-layout-ids.ts` → `STANDARD_PAGE_LAYOUT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS`).\n4. **An app-owned record page layout** — but it *replaces* the default layout, so it is unsuitable for \"every record page\" unless the app re-implements all fields (warning in `document-generator/.../document-record.page-layout.ts:13-16`).\n\n### Evidence-based recommendation\n\n**The \"Related\" panel is best built as an app `FRONT_COMPONENT` widget (or an app-owned additive tab containing it), not as a new native page-layout widget type** — unless the host itself takes ownership.\n\nRationale and constraints:\n- **Constraint:** a new widget *type* requires changes in the host's closed server enum + front dispatcher (`WidgetType.ts`, `WidgetConfigurationType.type.ts`, `WidgetContentRenderer.tsx:32-101`). That is a host/product change, not something an internal app can ship. If A2E wants `WidgetType.RELATED` to appear on *every* record page for *every* object, only the **host** can add it (e.g. mirroring how `TASKS/NOTES/FILES/TIMELINE` read fixed native relations via `WidgetTypeToRelationFieldName.ts:3-15`).\n- **Constraint:** backlinks are not implemented at all today (§3), and their computation source (mention nodes stored at save) exists only as BlockNote inline props (`MentionInlineContent.tsx:87-103`), with no index/query. Any surface needs new computation logic; a front component can encapsulate that logic in the app, whereas a native widget would force it into `twenty-front`.\n- **Constraint:** apps cannot attach a widget to an arbitrary existing page layout except via a *standalone tab the app declares* against a known standard layout id (the `a2e-chat` pattern). \"On every record page\" therefore means one tab declaration per standard page layout, or a host-wide widget.\n- **Precedent:** the `a2e-documents` app already renders heavy custom record-page content (including a \"child pages\" relation list) as a `FRONT_COMPONENT` widget inside its own record page (`document.page-layout.ts:37-45`; `document-page.front-component.tsx:767-820`). A \"Related\" panel follows that exact shape.\n- **Divergence:** if the panel must list links/backlinks for *any* object on the *host's* default record pages (M8d: \"on every record page\"), the app-tab-per-object approach is repetitive and leaks across apps; a host-owned widget type (or a host-rendered generic tab) is the cleaner fit. US-125 is the spike chartered to decide exactly this (`tasks/prd.json:508-510`).\n\n### Net answer\n- **Do not attempt a new app-owned widget type** — the system is closed (`WidgetType.ts:1-27`; `page-layout-widget.entity.ts:72-78`).\n- **If the panel is app logic:** ship it as a `FRONT_COMPONENT` widget (config `FrontComponentConfiguration`, `page-layout-widget-configuration.type.ts:140-144`) inside an app page layout/tab, following `a2e-documents` and `a2e-chat`. This is the only app-ownable widget payload.\n- **If the panel must be universal (every record page, every object):** it must be host-owned — either a new built-in `WidgetType` (host server+front change) or a host-rendered tab/widget. No app-level mechanism exists to inject a widget into every existing page layout generically.\n- The M8d backlink rune itself is unimplemented; the only durable hook available is the per-mention `recordId/objectMetadataId/objectNameSingular` stored in `MentionInlineContent` (`MentionInlineContent.tsx:87-103`), matched by `LinkToRecordPicker` insertion (`LinkToRecordPicker.tsx:72-84`).\n</task_result>\n</task>"
