        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f0bd32fd5ffe1N0OdE6eSkxOzA\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n# Native Polymorphic / Morph Relation Primitives — Research Report\n\nAll paths relative to `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite`. Read-only research; nothing modified.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The `attachment` object and its polymorphic target mechanism\n\n**Identity**\n- Core object name singular: `attachment` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/CoreObjectNameSingular.ts:5`\n- Object universal identifier: `STANDARD_OBJECT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS.attachment = '20202020-bd3d-4c60-8dca-571c71d4447a'` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object-universal-identifiers.constant.ts:9`\n- Morph group id: `STANDARD_OBJECTS.attachment.morphIds.targetMorphId.morphId = '20202020-f634-435d-ab8d-e1168b375c69'` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object.constant.ts:26-28`\n\n**The morph legs (fields that express \"target any record\")**\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/field-metadata/compute-attachment-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:422-652` declares seven `MORPH_RELATION` fields, all sharing the one `morphId`:\n\n| Field | targetObjectName | targetFieldName | onDelete / joinColumn |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `targetTask` (L422) | `task` | `attachments` | SET_NULL / `targetTaskId` |\n| `targetNote` (L455) | `note` | `attachments` | SET_NULL / `targetNoteId` |\n| `targetPerson` (L488) | `person` | `attachments` | CASCADE / `targetPersonId` |\n| `targetCompany` (L521) | `company` | `attachments` | CASCADE / `targetCompanyId` |\n| `targetOpportunity` (L554) | `opportunity` | `attachments` | CASCADE / `targetOpportunityId` |\n| `targetDashboard` (L587) | `dashboard` | `attachments` | CASCADE / `targetDashboardId` |\n| `targetWorkflow` (L620) | `workflow` | `attachments` | CASCADE / `targetWorkflowId` |\n\nEach is shaped as: `type: FieldMetadataType.MORPH_RELATION`, `morphId`, `targetObjectName`, `targetFieldName: 'attachments'`, `settings: { relationType: MANY_TO_ONE, onDelete, joinColumnName }`.\n\n- Field universal identifiers for these legs are derived by `getSystemRelationFieldUniversalIdentifier` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object-fields.constant.ts:174-243` (attachment block at 162-244).\n- **How a record references it:** the *inverse* side `attachments` is declared as a normal `RELATION` (ONE_TO_MANY) on every target object, e.g. `note.attachments` — `standard-object-fields.constant.ts:817-825`; for `dashboard`/`workflow`/`task` etc. the same pattern. Each attachment row stores exactly one non-null FK column among `target<X>Id`; the \"which object\" is encoded by *which* column is populated, not by a type/discriminator column.\n\n---\n\n## 2. General morph relation machinery\n\n**Primitive type names / shapes**\n- `FieldMetadataType.MORPH_RELATION` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/FieldMetadataType.ts:13`\n- `RelationAndMorphRelationFieldMetadataType` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/RelationAndMorphRelationFieldMetadataType.ts:3-5`\n- `FieldMetadataRelationSettings` includes `junctionTargetFieldId?: SerializedRelation` and the comment *\"For MORPH_RELATION fields, morphRelations already contains all targets\"* — `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/FieldMetadataSettings.ts:52-59`, mapped at `:81`.\n- `FieldMetadataUniversalSettings<T>` = `FormatRecordSerializedRelationProperties<FieldMetadataSettings<T>>` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/FieldMetadataUniversalSettings.ts:5-7`\n\n**Persisted shape — there is NO `morphRelations` array and no `morphTargetUniversalIdentifier` field in the DB.** Morph relations are stored as **one field row per target**, grouped by `morphId`:\n- `FieldMetadataEntity.morphId` column + DB check `\"type\" = 'MORPH_RELATION' AND \"morphId\" IS NOT NULL` — `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/field-metadata/field-metadata.entity.ts:48-51, 221-226`\n- `FlatFieldMetadata<T>` derives from `FieldMetadataEntity` — `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/flat-field-metadata/types/flat-field-metadata.type.ts:6-13`\n- The GraphQL `morphRelations: [RelationDTO]` is **computed**, not stored — resolver at `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/field-metadata/field-metadata.resolver.ts:323-342`, using `resolveMorphRelationsFromFlatFieldMetadata` (`.../flat-field-metadata/utils/resolve-morph-relations-from-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:19-32`) and `findAllOthersMorphRelationFlatFieldMetadatasOrThrow` (`.../find-all-others-morph-relation-flat-field-metadatas-or-throw.util.ts:21-25`).\n- Dataloader: `MorphRelationLoaderPayload` / `createMorphRelationLoader` — `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/dataloaders/dataloader.service.ts:58, 240-268`.\n- `RelationDTO` shape — `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/field-metadata/dtos/relation.dto.ts:16-38` (`type`, `sourceObjectMetadata`, `targetObjectMetadata`, `sourceFieldMetadata`, `targetFieldMetadata`).\n- Shared \"flat\" view of a morph leg: `FieldSharedMorphRelation = { type; targetObjectMetadata: { id; nameSingular; namePlural } }` and `FieldShared.morphRelations?` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/utils/filter/turnRecordFilterIntoGqlOperationFilter.ts:89-105`.\n\n**Naming convention**\n- `computeMorphRelationFlatFieldName` → `<fieldName><TargetSingular>` (M2O) / `<fieldName><TargetsPlural>` (O2M) — `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/field-metadata/utils/compute-morph-relation-flat-field-name.util.ts:16-33`\n- Isomorphic twin for GraphQL: `computeMorphRelationGqlFieldName` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/utils/fieldMetadata/compute-morph-relation-gql-field-name.ts:16-33`\n\n**Creation / validation**\n- `CreateFieldInput.morphRelationsCreationPayload?: RelationCreationPayload[]` — `.../dtos/create-field.input.ts:47`; update variant `morphRelationsUpdatePayload` — `.../dtos/update-field.input.ts:45`\n- `fromMorphRelationCreateFieldInputToFlatFieldMetadatas` requires payload, validates, generates **one `morphId = v4()`** and one relation pair per target — `.../utils/from-morph-relation-create-field-input-to-flat-field-metadatas.util.ts:44-126` (`const morphId = v4()` at L87)\n- `validateMorphRelationCreationPayload` — `.../validators/utils/validate-morph-relation-creation-payload.util.ts:26-163`: payload non-empty; **all same relation type** (L46-66); **must not target source object** (L75-89); **targets must be distinct objects** (L91-105).\n- `validateMorphRelationFlatFieldMetadata` — `.../validators/utils/validate-morph-relation-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`: **\"A morph relation field can only target a RELATION field\"** (L39-51), source ≠ target (L58-67), `morphId` required (L69-75).\n- Pair generation sets `morphId` only on the MORPH_RELATION leg and `null` on the RELATION leg — `.../utils/generate-morph-or-relation-flat-field-metadata-pair.util.ts:128-131, 185-197`.\n- `morphId` exposed on the DTO — `.../dtos/field-metadata.dto.ts:148`; `isMorphOrRelationFieldMetadataType` gate in `.../utils/is-morph-or-relation-field-metadata-type.util`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Objects currently using morph relations\n\nDeclared in `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object.constant.ts` (one `morphIds.targetMorphId.morphId` per holder):\n\n| Holder object | morphId | targets | source:line |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `attachment` | `20202020-f634-...` | task, note, person, company, opportunity, dashboard, workflow | `:26-28` |\n| `calendarEventTarget` | `676e9f68-7b5c-41e6-b46d-2fb9527b7051` | person, company, opportunity | `:247-249` |\n| `messageThreadTarget` | `e85e853d-c26e-41b3-bec0-7afc4bdbc2f7` | person, company, opportunity | `:659-661` |\n| `noteTarget` | `20202020-f635-435d-ab8d-e1168b375c70` | person, company, opportunity | `:751-753` |\n| `taskTarget` | `20202020-f636-435d-ab8d-e1168b375c71` | person, company, opportunity | `:1094` |\n| `timelineActivity` | `20202020-9a2b-4c3d-a4e5-f6a7b8c9d0e1` | person, company, opportunity, task, note, workflow, workflowVersion, workflowRun, dashboard, messageList, messageCampaign | `:1137-1139` |\n\n- Field builders: attachment (above), `compute-note-target-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:275-373`, `compute-task-target-...`, `compute-calendar-event-target-...`, `compute-message-thread-target-...`, `build-standard-target-flat-field-metadatas.util.ts:270-356` (shared person/company/opportunity target builder), `compute-timeline-activity-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:429-742`.\n- **Default/auto-provisioned morph holders:** `DEFAULT_RELATIONS_OBJECTS_STANDARD_IDS = ['timelineActivity','attachment','noteTarget','taskTarget']` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/default-relations-object-standard-ids.constant.ts:3-8`.\n- **`timelineActivity` also carries a legacy discriminator-column polymorphic mechanism** (distinct from morph): `linkedRecordCachedName`, `linkedRecordId`, `linkedObjectMetadataId` — `standard-object-fields.constant.ts:152-160`; entity at `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/timeline/standard-objects/timeline-activity.workspace-entity.ts:24-26`. This is the old \"targetObjectMetadataId + targetRecordId\" pattern. No field literally named `targetObjectMetadataId`/`targetRecordId` exists on attachment; those names appear on `navigationMenuItem` (unrelated) and in `metadata-event-publisher.ts:127-147` (webhook payload).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Declaring a morph relation in APP metadata\n\n**Manifest types** (`packages/twenty-shared/src/application/fieldManifestType.ts:48-64`):\n```ts\nRelationFieldManifest = {\n  type, name, label, ...\n  relationTargetFieldMetadataUniversalIdentifier: string;\n  relationTargetObjectMetadataUniversalIdentifier: string;\n  universalSettings: FieldMetadataUniversalSettings<T>;\n} & ([T] extends [MORPH_RELATION] ? { morphId: string } : { morphId?: undefined });\n```\nA morph relation is therefore **not** an array in app metadata either: the app declares **one `defineField` per morph target**, all sharing the same `morphId` and each pointing at a distinct target object + its inverse RELATION field.\n\n**Real app example** (`packages/twenty-apps/public/last-contact`): `src/fields/last-contact-item-message.field.ts:15-36` and `last-contact-item-calendar-event.field.ts` share `LAST_CONTACT_ITEM_MORPH_ID`; `company-*` share `COMPANY_LAST_CONTACT_ITEM_MORPH_ID`; `opportunity-*` share `OPPORTUNITY_LAST_CONTACT_ITEM_MORPH_ID` (constants at `src/constants/universal-identifiers.ts:38-39, 64-65, 77-78`). Each declares `morphId`, target object universal identifier (`message`/`calendarEvent`), inverse target field universal identifier, and `universalSettings: { relationType: MANY_TO_ONE, onDelete, joinColumnName }`.\n\n**App-owned objects can declare morph relations:** `ObjectManifest.fields: ObjectFieldManifest[]` and `ObjectFieldManifest = DistributiveOmit<FieldManifest<T>, 'objectUniversalIdentifier'>` (`packages/twenty-shared/src/application/objectManifestType.ts:24`, `.../objectFieldManifest.type.ts:8-10`). The field union includes morph, and `morphId` is allowed inside object-declared fields. The SDK only forbids `isUnique` on relation/morph fields (`packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/fields/validate-fields.ts:39-48`). No in-repo `defineObject` currently declares a morph field (only standalone `fields/` files), but the types permit it.\n\n**Can morph targets include app-owned objects? YES — and it is the designed default.**\n- On creation of **every object not owned by `twenty-standard`**, the engine auto-provisions the forward RELATION field on the new object plus the reverse **MORPH_RELATION** field on the four holders. Side-effect handler: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/metadata-side-effect/handlers/object-metadata/services/object-system-relations-on-create-side-effect-handler.service.ts:28-113` (note L34 explicitly names \"the four standard relation objects\"); builder: `.../object-metadata/utils/build-system-relation-flat-field-metadatas-for-object.util.ts:45-124` with `MORPH_ID_BY_STANDARD_OBJECT_NAME_SINGULAR` for `timelineActivity | attachment | noteTarget | taskTarget` (`:22-28`). The reverse field is named `target<ObjectSingular>` with join column `<reverseFieldName>Id` (`:56-61`), type `MORPH_RELATION` (`:93`).\n- The 2-38 backfill explicitly targets app/custom objects and skips only standard-app objects: `packages/twenty-server/src/database/commands/upgrade-version-command/2-38/utils/build-missing-object-system-relation-candidates.util.ts:94-102`, deriving existing morph targets via `morphId` (`:70-84`).\n- A2E uses this: `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-projects/src/page-layouts/project.page-layout.ts:182-198` references the \"native attachments widget (reads the record's polymorphic `attachments` relation, auto-provisioned on app objects)\".\n- `validate-morph-relation-*` impose **no** standard-only restriction on targets.\n- Note: auto-provisioning covers only `timelineActivity/attachment/noteTarget/taskTarget`. `calendarEventTarget` and `messageThreadTarget` are **not** in that list, so app objects are not automatically morph targets there (must be declared explicitly).\n\n**App-level junction marker:** `universalSettings.junctionTargetFieldUniversalIdentifier` on the ONE_TO_MANY owning side — example `packages/twenty-apps/fixtures/rich-app/src/fields/post-card-recipients-on-post-card.field.ts:21-24`; converted to flat `junctionTargetFieldId` at `.../from-universal-settings-to-flat-field-metadata-settings.util.ts:39-64`.\n\n**Constraints / install-order**\n- Target inverse must be a RELATION, distinct objects, one relation type, `morphId` required (validation utils above).\n- Manifest conversion requires both `relationTargetFieldMetadataUniversalIdentifier` and `relationTargetObjectMetadataUniversalIdentifier` or it throws — `.../converters/from-field-manifest-to-universal-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:37-52`.\n- At **install/run time**, unresolved universal identifiers throw: `Relation target field metadata not found ...` / `Relation target object metadata not found ...` — `.../workspace-migration-runner/action-handlers/field/services/utils/from-universal-flat-field-metadata-to-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:73-100`. So an app morph relation targeting another app's object requires that other app installed first (or the target declared in the same manifest). Same-manifest pairs are bundled into one create action via `aggregate-relation-field-pairs.util.ts:37-66`.\n- `junctionTargetFieldUniversalIdentifier` unresolved also throws — `from-universal-settings-to-flat-field-metadata-settings.util.ts:51-59`.\n- Export rule: a morph field without `morphId` is not exportable — `.../application-manifest/utils/get-unsupported-relation-field-reason.util.ts:34-39`.\n- Cross-app prerequisite precedent (ordering): `a2e-projects` declares A2E Documents as a \"hard install prerequisite\" — `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-projects/src/page-layouts/project.page-layout.ts:200-209`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Federation / inverse / backlinks — how related records are computed today\n\nThere is **no primitive literally named \"backlink\"**. The generic inverse/related capability is implemented as the **junction** + morph-relation machinery in `twenty-front`.\n\n**GraphQL fetch of morph values** (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/graphql/record-gql-fields/utils/generateDepthRecordGqlFieldsFromFields.ts:88-123`): for each `fieldMetadata.morphRelations[]` it computes gql field `<fieldName><TargetSingular>` via `computeMorphRelationGqlFieldName` and nests target identifier fields. Same pattern in `generateJunctionRelationGqlFields.ts`.\n\n**Reading values** — `recordStoreMorphOneToManyValueWithObjectNameFamilySelector.ts:18-47` maps each morph relation to `{ objectNameSingular, value }` using the computed gql field name. Consumed by `useGetMorphRelationRelatedRecordsWithObjectNameSingular` (`.../record-detail-section/relation/components/hooks/...:6-58`).\n\n**Junction resolution (the reusable \"link any record\" logic)**\n- Types: `JunctionConfig` / `ValidJunctionConfig` / `ValidResolvedJunctionConfig` — `.../record-field/ui/utils/junction/types/{JunctionConfig,ValidJunctionConfig,ValidResolvedJunctionConfig}.ts`\n- `getJunctionConfig.ts:18-125` — finds the junction object, its source field (RELATION or MORPH_RELATION), and the target field; infers legacy morph junction when unlabeled + exactly one morph target; marks `isMorphRelation = targetField.type === MORPH_RELATION`.\n- `resolveJunctionConfig.ts:60-139` + `resolveReverseJunctionConfig.ts:92-279` — forward/reverse/ambiguous/invalid resolution; configured via `settings.junctionTargetFieldId` (`hasJunctionTargetFieldId.ts:16-27`, `isConfiguredJunctionRelationField.ts:5-9`, `isUsableJunctionConfig.ts`).\n- Object-scoped morph junction (`note.noteTargets` etc.): `getObjectMorphJunctionConfig.ts:20-83` (yields `junctionField`, `sourceField`, `sourceJoinColumnName`, `junctionObjectMetadata`), hook `useObjectMorphJunctionConfig` / `useObjectMorphJunctionConfigOrThrow`.\n- `categorizeRelationFields.ts:49-86` splits fields into `inlineRelationFields`, `junctionRelationFields`, `boxedRelationFields` for the record detail page.\n\n**Related/backlink UI surfaces**\n- Record detail sections: `RecordDetailRelationSection.tsx`, `RecordDetailMorphRelationSection.tsx`, `RecordDetailRelationRecordsList.tsx`, dropdowns `RecordDetailMorphRelationSectionDropdown*.tsx` (all under `.../record-field-list/record-detail-section/relation/components/`).\n- Page-layout widgets: `WidgetRelationsHeader.tsx:19-42` renders `RecordTargetsInlineCell.tsx:24-108` (the morph junction picker, e.g. attachment targets) in the record page header; `FieldWidgetMorphRelationField.tsx` / `FieldWidgetMorphRelationCard.tsx` render related record chips/cards; `FieldWidgetJunctionRelationCard.tsx` / `FieldWidgetRelationRecordsCard.tsx`; `FieldWidgetRelationTable.tsx`.\n- `useFieldWidgetJunctionRelationRecords.ts`, `resolveFieldWidgetJunctionConfig.ts`, `getFieldWidgetRelationTraversal.ts:34-57` (morph junctions get no embedded view — L33 comment).\n- Related-record actions: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/hooks/useRelatedRecordActions.ts:14`.\n- Cell display: `MorphRelationManyToOneFieldDisplay.tsx`; record pickers use `RecordPickerPickableMorphItem` (`SingleRecordPickerMenuItem.tsx`, `MultipleRecordPicker*.tsx`).\n\n**Front-end morph field type**: `FieldMetadataItem.morphRelations?: FieldMetadataItemRelation[]` and `morphId?: string | null` — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/types/FieldMetadataItem.ts:36, 43`; `FieldMetadataItemRelation` shape at `.../FieldMetadataItemRelation.ts:5-17` (`type`, `source/targetFieldMetadata`, `source/targetObjectMetadata`).\n\n---\n\n## Bottom line for a generic \"link any record\" junction\n\n- The reusable native primitive is `FieldMetadataType.MORPH_RELATION`: a **set of per-target relation fields sharing one `morphId`**, each pointing at a distinct target object, with the inverse RELATION field on the target. There is no stored target-type discriminator column; the populated join column identifies the target.\n- `attachment`, `noteTarget`, `taskTarget`, `timelineActivity` are the four **auto-provisioned morph holders** for every non-standard object — this is precisely a generic \"link any record\" junction already in place, and app-owned objects are automatically morph targets there.\n- App metadata declares each morph leg as a `RelationFieldManifest` with `morphId` + target object/field universal identifiers; app-owned objects may declare morph relations, and app-owned objects may be morph targets (explicitly, and automatically for the four default holders).\n- Install is universal-identifier-based: target object and target inverse field must exist either in the same manifest or already in the workspace, otherwise install throws (`from-universal-flat-field-metadata-to-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:73-100`); cross-app morph targets therefore imply an install-order prerequisite.\n- The front-end \"related/backlink\" experience is the **junction** resolution layer (`resolveJunctionConfig` / `resolveReverseJunctionConfig` / `getObjectMorphJunctionConfig`) plus morph display widgets; no separate backlink primitive exists.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
